  "result": "The gate never judged my work. Both runs returned `SCOPE_VIOLATION`, so the rule and witnesses haven't been built or tested. The files it flagged aren't ones I touched. They're the agent runtime's temp files under `.runtime/tmp/claude-154266/…`: my own gate-command output, output from the concurrent LVMC_11_18_020 and LVMC_11_30_050 sessions, and a `cache-break-state-*.json`. Every gate run writes a new output file there, so running again wouldn't help. I stopped after 2 of the 6 runs.\n\n**What I wrote, in the two node files only:**\n- **Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_16_060.lean`):\n  - **Subject:** must be a vehicle under the `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle` aggregate.\n  - **When the rule applies:** the subject is on a highway, and no speed limit sign of kind maximum, structure_maximum or zone governs a lane or other travel region it occupies.\n  - **Obligation:** the subject's speed is at most 25 mph, written as `Units.mph 25`.\n  - **Choices of my own:** none, so `narrowings` is empty.\n- **Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_16_060.lean`): the four planned scenarios plus three extra branches.\n\n  | witness | scene | expected |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | forbid | no sign, 35 mph | violated |\n  | permit | no sign, 20 mph | compliant |\n  | idle | 45 mph maximum sign governs the subject's lane | not applicable |\n  | blind | sign present, what it governs is not observed, 35 mph | unknown |\n  | branch_1 | minimum sign on the subject's lane, 35 mph | violated |\n  | branch_2 | maximum sign on the next lane only, 35 mph | violated |\n  | branch_3 | subject off the highway, 35 mph | not applicable |\n\n**Fix needed in the harness:** the scope check should ignore `.runtime/tmp/`, or the agent temp directory should sit outside the tree the gate compares. The harness re-runs the gate after this session, but it may hit the same problem if other sessions' temp files are still there.\n\n`task_result.md` in the working directory has both gate runs, the choices, and why I finished.",
